# Pinned major version of the clang tooling for this repository.
#
# Both clang-format and clang-tidy are read from this pin, by build/lint/format
# scripts and by CI, so every machine produces the same result.
#
# WHY PIN. Formatting is a consensus artifact: two versions disagree on output,
# so an unpinned clang-format makes `--check` fail depending on who ran it.
# Linting is a blocking gate: a newer clang-tidy adds checks, and an unpinned
# one turns a routine package upgrade into a red build on an unrelated commit.
#
# UPGRADING is a deliberate commit of its own:
#   1. Bump this file.
#   2. Re-derive the alias list in .clang-tidy from the new version's
#      documentation. Alias direction changes between releases -- verify no
#      alias and its canonical target are both enabled.
#   3. Run python3 dev.py format and commit the reformat separately from any behaviour
#      change, so review can skip it.
#   4. Fix or record every new finding. Never widen the deviation budget to
#      absorb them silently.
20
